      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "1. Verify that the Zenith SmartHub is powered on and confirm that the primary status indicator light is displaying a solid green, indicating active power reception.\n2. Inspect the physical Ethernet cable connection at both the Hub's WAN port and the router's LAN port, ensuring the locking mechanism is fully engaged and no visible damage exists on the cable itself.\n3. Perform a complete power cycle of your home router by disconnecting the power cord for a minimum of sixty seconds, allowing all internal capacitors to fully discharge before reconnecting.\n4. Access the SmartHub configuration interface and meticulously re-enter the Wi-Fi network name (SSID) and security password, paying close attention to case sensitivity and special characters.\n5. Temporarily disable any active firewall rules or VPN client software running on your primary network gateway device to definitively isolate the connectivity issue from local security protocols.\n6. Check the router's administrative interface to confirm that the SmartHub's MAC address has not been inadvertently blocked by MAC filtering settings.\n7. Attempt to connect the SmartHub using a different, known-good Ethernet cable to eliminate the possibility of a faulty cable component.",
      "source": "target",
